{"name":"Tassel","hex":"#c6884a","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tassel","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A ball-shaped bunch of plaited or otherwise entangled threads from which at one end protrudes a cord on which the ball is hung, and which may have loose, dangling threads at the other end (often used as decoration along the bottom of garments, curtains or other hangings).","The panicle on a male plant of maize, which consists of loose threads with anthers on them."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To adorn with tassels.","To put forth a tassel or flower."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tassel"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tassel","blocks":[{"text":"A tassel is a finishing feature in fabric and clothing decoration. It is a universal ornament that is seen in varying versions in many cultures around the globe."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/Tassel2.svg/330px-Tassel2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tassel","wikidata":"Q1194132"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Orna118-Quasten.png/500px-Orna118-Quasten.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Orna118-Quasten.png/500px-Orna118-Quasten.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Illustration of various tassels, from A Handbook of Ornament, by Franz Sales Meyer","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOrna118-Quasten.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/Tester_bed_%28lit_%C3%A0_la_duchesse_en_imp%C3%A9riale%29_MET_DP155162.jpg/500px-Tester_bed_%28lit_%C3%A0_la_duchesse_en_imp%C3%A9riale%29_MET_DP155162.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb